B10a — Restored evidence of 92 reviewed disposition rows
========================================================

Found on 2026-10-13 by the L10 work. Restored on 2026-10-14 (+0800).

Scope: the evidence paths of tests/contracts/benchmark-program-dispositions.json.
92 rows (8 LLVM, 77 GCC torture, 7 c-testsuite) cited 82 files that no longer
existed, in 152 citations. classify_program makes such a row a compiler
failure, even when the original program passes. Each cited file now has a
retained copy, and only the 152 path strings changed. No disposition, reason,
source hash, original command, outcome, receipt or historical count changes.
No row needed a new measurement, so no compiler ran.

Where the evidence went:
  docs/notebook/benchmark-applicability.md (61 rows): commit 5d8a1522 moved
    the dated notes to docs/archive/notebook on 2026-10-06 without a change of
    content. Commit 1c11c0d3 then deepened 17 relative links by one level.
  docs/evoir-spec.md (4 rows): commit 652340da renamed it to spec/evoir.md on
    2026-10-06. Commit 598ec28c archived its Appendix D, which holds the cited
    review rulings, as docs/archive/notebook/evoir-spec-review-20261001.md.
    Commit 55d5bd58 (Revision 2.0.0) then removed that appendix.
  .build/ladder/torture/... and .build/ladder/ctest/... (80 files, 87
    citations in 85 rows): the pinned checkouts that e0.fetch makes. The
    runs of 2026-09-27 still used them. The present .build/ladder directory
    was created on 2026-10-06 18:41 +0800 (its birth time). The old torture,
    c-testsuite and LLVM trees are gone.
    The cleanup records .evidence/storage-cleanup-20261004 and
    .evidence/storage-cleanup-20261011 do not list them. No local copy
    remains in the repository, the home directory or the temporary
    directories.

Methods (the word in parentheses in the row list):
  archive   Cite the tracked moved file
            docs/archive/notebook/benchmark-applicability.md, blob 4a40145c4571,
            SHA256 28ed76a29293999dc94ec7c86fd3aceaf9de00fe1d7dfe0f1e9039bc9e6d6f3b.
            It equals the pre-move blob 60e93b69f41d apart from 17 link
            prefixes (../../ to ../../../). The note names all 61 citing
            programs. docs/archive/README.md says that tools and receipts
            can still name an archived path.
  history   Restore the last version at the cited path from Git:
            git show 20363d8e:docs/evoir-spec.md (the parent of 652340da),
            EvoIR Revision 1.9.116 of 2026-10-01, 616,844 bytes.
            It equals 652340da:spec/evoir.md. Its Appendix D equals the
            archived review note byte for byte. The current spec/evoir.md
            (Revision 2.3.0) has no Appendix D, but its body still makes an
            argument other than 0 to __builtin_return_address E2913 and
            integer-complex division E2948.
  upstream  Restore the pinned original source byte for byte, with
            git cat-file blob COMMIT:PATH in a fresh clone:
              torture  gcc-mirror/gcc tag releases/gcc-16.2.0, commit
                       78d4ac73dd391005b895a6148cd9831e28e1208b
                       (sourceCommits.torture; 1,692 execute programs)
              ctest    c-testsuite/c-testsuite commit
                       5c7275656d751de0e68b2d340a95b5681858ed07
                       (sourceCommits.ctest)
            A program's own source equals the sourceSha256 of its torture or
            ctest row. LLVM rows cite the source of their reviewed equivalent
            torture program. The two included gcc.dg/tree-ssa files equal the
            blob ids of the pinned tree.

New evidence directory .evidence/disposition-evidence-20261013/ (untracked,
like all of .evidence/):
  torture/gcc/testsuite/  73 GCC sources: 71 execute, 2 gcc.dg/tree-ssa
  ctest/tests/single-exec/  7 c-testsuite sources
  docs/evoir-spec.md      the restored specification
  manifest.json           each old path, new path, method and identity
  tools/                  the restore, source, validation and record scripts
  logs/                   their outputs and the unit test log
  SHA256SUMS              every other file of the directory
The scratch clones and the LLVM tree are not kept. The commands below make
them again.

Commands (B is a scratch directory, R the repository root,
N = R/.evidence/disposition-evidence-20261013,
C = 2919e55176a572ee085cb46b291c47b7092c363e and L = B/llvm/llvm-test-suite-C):
  git -c http.version=HTTP/1.1 clone -q --filter=blob:none --sparse \
    --depth 1 --branch releases/gcc-16.2.0 \
    https://github.com/gcc-mirror/gcc.git B/gcc
  git -C B/gcc sparse-checkout set gcc/testsuite/gcc.c-torture/execute
  git -c http.version=HTTP/1.1 clone -q --depth 1 \
    https://github.com/c-testsuite/c-testsuite.git B/ctest
  curl -sSL --http1.1 --fail https://codeload.github.com/llvm/llvm-test-suite/tar.gz/C \
    | tee >(shasum -a 256) | tar -xzf - -C B/llvm llvm-test-suite-C/SingleSource
    The stream SHA256 is
    415106c9962e07a24326ad9173bbecd4215f6dee49bce9aec5181d75d07db770,
    the pin of tools/ladder/llvm-test-suite.py.
  python3 -I N/tools/restore_evidence.py R B/gcc B/ctest manifest.json --apply
  python3 -I N/tools/verify_sources.py R B/gcc B/ctest L
  python3 -I N/tools/validate_rows.py R B/gcc B/ctest L
  python3 -m unittest discover -s tools/ladder/tests

Source identity: the sourceSha256 of all 1,068 rows equals the SHA256 of the
re-fetched pinned source (838 LLVM, 223 torture, 7 c-testsuite).

Validation: validate_rows.py runs the adapters' own code on every row. LLVM
rows go through program_disposition of tools/ladder/llvm-test-suite.py.
Torture and c-testsuite rows go through e0.classify_program, which
program_disposition also calls. Outcomes and original commands come from the
latest retained full runs: .evidence/ladder/llvm-test-suite/20260927T085137Z,
.evidence/ladder/e0/20260927T082713Z (ctest) and
.evidence/ladder/e0/20260927T084053Z (torture). This checks the evidence,
source and command binding. It is not a new replay.
  Before: 92 rows return dispositionError "reviewed disposition has missing
    evidence, changed source or invalid label" and compiler-failure.
  After: no row returns dispositionError. 1,067 dispositions equal those of
    the retained runs. The other row, LLVM pr23135, is not-applicable under
    the L10 rule of commit 2de32fcf; its run recorded compiler-failure.
  After, by suite:
    llvm-test-suite  PASS 143, not-applicable 665, FP-deferred 30
    torture          PASS 114, not-applicable 85, FP-deferred 21,
                     oracle-unusable 3
    ctest            PASS 7
  16 of the 92 rows are FP-deferred but name no still-deferred feature: no
  deferredFeatures (ctest 00113, 00119, 00123, 00174, 00175, 00195, torture
  20000603-1, 20000731-1, 20001017-1, stdarg-4, LLVM stdarg-4) or binary128
  only (torture and LLVM 20040709-1 and 20040709-2, ctest 00204). Their
  originals passed in the retained runs, so the validator returns PASS for
  them. If a replay does not pass one of them, it returns compiler-failure.
  The B10 replay decides them.
  python3 -m unittest discover -s tools/ladder/tests: 575 tests, OK, 9
  skipped. The new test test_every_reviewed_row_cites_existing_evidence
  failed with 152 missing citations before the restore. It passes after it.

